699649095535, -0.013384589925408363, 0.07712797075510025, -0.003192781237885356, 0.021238790825009346, -0.09516525268554688, 0.042056165635585785, 0.007447861135005951, -0.014043185859918594, -0.03297380357980728, -0.01082236785441637, -0.098833829164505, -0.007686315104365349, -0.026625139638781548, 0.03669216111302376, -0.08650170266628265, 0.02668796107172966, -0.0014753545401617885, 0.03545010834932327, 0.07287980616092682, -0.046161264181137085, -0.04076995328068733, -0.051120806485414505, 0.0037389930803328753, 0.022327734157443047, -0.04826181009411812, 0.0327586755156517, 0.005880360491573811, -0.040452342480421066, -0.014880175702273846], "response": "<p>A fever is a body defense mechanism that occurs when the body's thermostat, or hypothalamus, resets at a higher temperature in response to an infection or illness. This can be caused by a variety of factors, including viral or bacterial infections, allergic reactions, autoimmune diseases, trauma, cancer, and excessive exposure to the sun.</p><p>When a fever occurs, the body's metabolic rate increases, causing the body to produce more heat. This can lead to a range of symptoms, including:</p><p>- A high body temperature, usually above 100.4\u00b0F (38\u00b0C)</p><p>- Chills or shivering</p><p>- Sweating</p><p>- Headache</p><p>- Fatigue</p><p>- Loss of appetite</p><p>- Muscle aches and pains</p><p>Fever is a natural response to infection, and it can help the body fight off the invading bacteria or viruses. However, in some cases, fever can be a sign of a more serious underlying condition, such as meningitis or sepsis.</p><p>There are different types of fever, including:</p><p>- Acute fever: A short-term fever that lasts for a few days</p><p>- Chronic fever: A long-term fever that lasts for weeks or months</p><p>- Recurrent fever: A fever that occurs repeatedly over a period of time</p><p>Fever can be diagnosed using a thermometer, and treatment typically involves addressing the underlying cause of the fever. In some cases, medication may be prescribed to help reduce the fever and alleviate symptoms.</p><p>Fever is an important component of the immune response, and it plays a crucial role in helping the body fight off infection. However, it can also have some downsides, such as increasing the body's metabolic rate and oxygen consumption, which can be devastating for people with poor circulation.</p>"}, {"query": "what is scoliosis", "embedding": [-0.03563236445188522, -0.0003416870313230902, -0.09958000481128693, -0.045092225074768066, -0.026478394865989685, 0.040243227034807205, -0.04196831211447716, 0.018433216959238052, -0.019292348995804787, 0.02058292180299759, 0.038572899997234344, 0.11440828442573547, 0.0834319069981575, -0.013492655009031296, -0.10825448483228683, 0.005852419417351484, -0.04768678545951843, 0.015399018302559853, 0.0001327895006397739, 0.12053115665912628, -0.028363460674881935, 0.09296852350234985, -0.0872444286942482, 0.04270524904131889, -0.08095235377550125, -0.024040279909968376, -0.01677410863339901, -0.12163294851779938, -0.05888838320970535, 0.14267781376838684, -0.027051938697695732, 0.03628278523683548, 0.12566635012626648, -0.025790026411414146, -0.0028124451637268066, 0.02641630545258522, 0.045442018657922745, 0.04020972177386284, -0.032861918210983276, -0.02175615169107914, -0.060399431735277176, -0.06094185262918472, -0.00531228631734848, 0.025885019451379776, 0.07002582401037216, -0.01272605825215578, -0.00016949017299339175, 0.02311292104423046, 0.0035919276997447014, 0.04191310331225395, -0.044616103172302246, -0.04492250457406044, -0.018216891214251518, -0.0524640753865242, -0.017281142994761467, 0.06494472175836563, -0.03679705411195755, 0.06996413320302963, -0.04161636531352997, 0.0050694928504526615, 0.11129295825958252, -0.10774587094783783, 0.02552543394267559, 0.09253747761249542, 0.07425445318222046, 0.006740621291100979, 0.03458229824900627, -0.025523662567138672, 0.01596774533390999, 0.02913561277091503, 0.01251993328332